r-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141824" :question/id #uuid "09888709-a9b4-533c-9d2f-2499db44d07a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141824" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-6{y}^{2}+24y=21.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${y}^{2}-4y+4$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-4y+4=(y-2)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{y}^{2}+24y & =21 \\\\ -6({y}^{2}-4y) & =21 \\\\ -6({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y) & =21 \\\\ -6({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}) & =21 \\\\ -6[(y-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}] & =21 \\\\ -6[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =21 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2}+(-6)(-4) & =21 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2}+24 & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by subtracting $24$ from both sides and then dividing by $(-6),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6(y-2)^{2}+24 & =21 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2}+24-24 & =21-24 \\\\ -6(y-2)^{2} & =-3 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{(-3)}{(-6)} \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{(y-2)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\ |y-2| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ y & =2\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141824/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141817/selection/386391c3b9f8cc7def615f25bfc253e33b699c278b8308987eaf60eea4abe050" :answer/id #uuid "ee9aa992-a8b1-547d-900d-979b04a2592e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-4\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141817/selection/16cd3c41e709f592a21f0684d295a590eb2acceb83a0ea11122e032cf01ef136" :answer/id #uuid "9caf14c0-b4fa-5d48-89ec-d775d83d30f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141817/selection/a87a454601fa990848387114bb80e09ffbf3047349dbcfb32bba640bff7f931d" :answer/id #uuid "3a50c376-b492-596c-bf08-8ffc86366ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4\\pm \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141817/selection/a03c77a918101d619b7f1641322a96f0230944c3a1070f4904c20f91ba4e6b4a" :answer/id #uuid "f58c33a1-5462-5f19-aad5-b66430aaa939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141817/selection/f3f47e42edbf1a222e01bcfb61d44004e31825cf90dbf814dd1b35f51208fc52" :answer/id #uuid "c50124c8-3498-577a-872c-30befb238e18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141817/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06e7f7bf-2b78-50f2-8da6-e37a47f569c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141817/selection/a03c77a918101d619b7f1641322a96f0230944c3a1070f4904c20f91ba4e6b4a" :answer-field/choices ["q-141817/selection/386391c3b9f8cc7def615f25bfc253e33b699c278b8308987eaf60eea4abe050" "q-141817/selection/16cd3c41e709f592a21f0684d295a590eb2acceb83a0ea11122e032cf01ef136" "q-141817/selection/a87a454601fa990848387114bb80e09ffbf3047349dbcfb32bba640bff7f931d" "q-141817/selection/a03c77a918101d619b7f1641322a96f0230944c3a1070f4904c20f91ba4e6b4a" "q-141817/selection/f3f47e42edbf1a222e01bcfb61d44004e31825cf90dbf814dd1b35f51208fc52"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141817" :question/id #uuid "8f7fa964-2584-5183-90c8-a1b508a4a91d" :question/math-academy-id "q-141817" :question/problem "Solve the equation $5{y}^{2}-40y=-76.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${y}^{2}-8y+16$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-8y+16=(y-4)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-40y & =-76 \\\\ 5({y}^{2}-8y) & =-76 \\\\ 5({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 4y) & =-76 \\\\ 5({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 4y+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2}) & =-76 \\\\ 5[(y-4)^{2}-{4}^{2}] & =-76 \\\\ 5[(y-4)^{2}-16] & =-76 \\\\ 5(y-4)^{2}-80 & =-76\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by adding $80$ to both sides and then dividing by $5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(y-4)^{2}-80 & =-76 \\\\ 5(y-4)^{2}-80+80 & =-76+80 \\\\ 5(y-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{(y-4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{5}} \\\\ |y-4| & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ y & =4\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141817/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141817"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141829/selection/cb80d348360455fd90bbf92f56db68a3f2da925522d46b30caea53d713cd08fc" :answer/id #uuid "54506512-9306-549c-83ff-5db21741148f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141829/selection/f0cd9c4923b172fef70e816c72e650f10f7ae0addce838b2fdff335f4a68806b" :answer/id #uuid "961e56ab-bdab-5524-a27b-5ac33c23726c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141829/selection/c8ea15ead3b3f0e9b92ab35fa37b0a775bef1d12238eeb5f94e60639142d8403" :answer/id #uuid "ac6b5dd0-c339-5a33-bbd1-fc0cbd29c677" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141829/selection/5989620ff47eb5a4511612d2e11e628d0821fbe38e6ac695b4ca04b0cd47f3e8" :answer/id #uuid "ef4dc683-fc94-5c1d-abc0-33329f16b6d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141829/selection/123042c2eaeb6e6526941b1110100877e64e816a4c46cffffb72ce9bbfe7c5a7" :answer/id #uuid "0d7440a5-151b-5c7f-b511-4d43f5aaf154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141829/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba362a8f-3350-5525-9bf4-bf8e762c3f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141829/selection/123042c2eaeb6e6526941b1110100877e64e816a4c46cffffb72ce9bbfe7c5a7" :answer-field/choices ["q-141829/selection/cb80d348360455fd90bbf92f56db68a3f2da925522d46b30caea53d713cd08fc" "q-141829/selection/f0cd9c4923b172fef70e816c72e650f10f7ae0addce838b2fdff335f4a68806b" "q-141829/selection/c8ea15ead3b3f0e9b92ab35fa37b0a775bef1d12238eeb5f94e60639142d8403" "q-141829/selection/5989620ff47eb5a4511612d2e11e628d0821fbe38e6ac695b4ca04b0cd47f3e8" "q-141829/selection/123042c2eaeb6e6526941b1110100877e64e816a4c46cffffb72ce9bbfe7c5a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141829" :question/id #uuid "e1ccb300-e0da-5a40-bcbe-b429bc99ba4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141829" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-4{x}^{2}+4x=-2.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}-x+\\frac{1}{4}$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-x+\\frac{1}{4}={(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}^{2}+4x & =-2 \\\\ -4({x}^{2}-x) & =-2 \\\\ -4({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x) & =-2 \\\\ -4({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}) & =-2 \\\\ -4[{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}] & =-2 \\\\ -4[{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}] & =-2 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+(-4)(-\\frac{1}{4}) & =-2 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1 & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by subtracting $1$ from both sides and then dividing by $(-4),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1 & =-2 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1-1 & =-2-1 \\\\ -4{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =-3 \\\\ {(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{(-3)}{(-4)} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{1}{2}| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x-\\frac{1}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-141829/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141829"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141811/selection/27e2ca6437c68e0f89d7c5cf09ec19b3c0affd75a93d14271bbe8837d4da0c06" :answer/id #uuid "efb0ebe0-b67e-5a85-9acd-afcc26644c8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141811/selection/6c25dc0e74d970b24e0de07e871e9aa7865462c5748da2a0565ab61a5cadaf92" :answer/id #uuid "f9c8fdb5-df24-5cb9-86f1-3fcce01dc435" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{11}{2},\\,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141811/selection/957c1a2611eb2cc53df6b6dc00386571d5af4a27f5ea865a9f955723d1ee36f6" :answer/id #uuid "99db0a40-555f-5b7b-b99c-43c02083233e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{11}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141811/selection/98830a5e7685109375c9f491d7fa1782601131b22176084e518438c4bd1173d4" :answer/id #uuid "14d2ed25-01e0-50c9-88c5-9c13a05d263f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3\\pm \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141811/selection/5d7fa7f8432aad45215f029e93932601644a7fcfc98577100363660ee3a64225" :answer/id #uuid "1ad54a88-511d-5fa8-8780-2452d4185cf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141811/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "55e58c50-30d6-598a-a4c4-a55373f39bf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141811/selection/957c1a2611eb2cc53df6b6dc00386571d5af4a27f5ea865a9f955723d1ee36f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-141811/selection/27e2ca6437c68e0f89d7c5cf09ec19b3c0affd75a93d14271bbe8837d4da0c06" "q-141811/selection/6c25dc0e74d970b24e0de07e871e9aa7865462c5748da2a0565ab61a5cadaf92" "q-141811/selection/957c1a2611eb2cc53df6b6dc00386571d5af4a27f5ea865a9f955723d1ee36f6" "q-141811/selection/98830a5e7685109375c9f491d7fa1782601131b22176084e518438c4bd1173d4" "q-141811/selection/5d7fa7f8432aad45215f029e93932601644a7fcfc98577100363660ee3a64225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141811" :question/id #uuid "6cd3a3fd-0ec4-5982-bdba-cd236ee44004" :question/math-academy-id "q-141811" :question/problem "Solve the equation $4{x}^{2}+24x=-11.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}+6x+9$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+6x+9=(x+3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+24x & =-11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+6x) & =-11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x) & =-11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}) & =-11 \\\\ 4[(x+3)^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =-11 \\\\ 4[(x+3)^{2}-9] & =-11 \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}-36 & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by adding $36$ to both sides and then dividing by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+3)^{2}-36 & =-11 \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}-36+36 & =-11+36 \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{(x+3)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\ |x+3| & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ x+3 & =\\pm \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ x & =-3\\pm \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{11}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141811/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141811"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141826/selection/930bfe7c7fadbc28df28bddd16b2a9f73b091596b0474885ac4832451dfe9910" :answer/id #uuid "38b1ba8b-fe39-500e-b26b-4cd7b3d475fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3\\pm \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141826/selection/0e56581e3adc81d0b105b113b275755906945b8abf41fde5163afb54ad2b5666" :answer/id #uuid "40492123-d936-598a-8f12-00dd601bd92a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-6\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141826/selection/905deeb33575460ec35625d388b16fe201050f47d3f16bd7528841ca29f6fee2" :answer/id #uuid "ced993ea-00b7-5c99-8112-acdbc1b7d0f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141826/selection/ff21b7071b9846c3f4f0f2ecac6d3ef496f57be9a18a4b42ea9c636aadb4d45f" :answer/id #uuid "55ccd822-036a-5651-a299-b69613cf91d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141826/selection/eee9d04169d73c9b6aac67f94dbed44923a58ddb2e4762fdec79a09acf18fbc8" :answer/id #uuid "6a94c0ee-849d-599b-8982-eb0ab0d4dcfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6\\pm \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141826/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06e2891d-e958-5ac9-85b5-7a611a692cbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141826/selection/ff21b7071b9846c3f4f0f2ecac6d3ef496f57be9a18a4b42ea9c636aadb4d45f" :answer-field/choices ["q-141826/selection/930bfe7c7fadbc28df28bddd16b2a9f73b091596b0474885ac4832451dfe9910" "q-141826/selection/0e56581e3adc81d0b105b113b275755906945b8abf41fde5163afb54ad2b5666" "q-141826/selection/905deeb33575460ec35625d388b16fe201050f47d3f16bd7528841ca29f6fee2" "q-141826/selection/ff21b7071b9846c3f4f0f2ecac6d3ef496f57be9a18a4b42ea9c636aadb4d45f" "q-141826/selection/eee9d04169d73c9b6aac67f94dbed44923a58ddb2e4762fdec79a09acf18fbc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141826" :question/id #uuid "cd4c0b98-656e-57bb-9139-ee0693930845" :question/math-academy-id "q-141826" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-7{y}^{2}-42y=62.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${y}^{2}+6y+9$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+6y+9=(y+3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7{y}^{2}-42y & =62 \\\\ -7({y}^{2}+6y) & =62 \\\\ -7({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 3y) & =62 \\\\ -7({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 3y+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}) & =62 \\\\ -7[(y+3)^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =62 \\\\ -7[(y+3)^{2}-9] & =62 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2}+(-7)(-9) & =62 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2}+63 & =62\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolating the perfect square by subtracting $63$ from both sides and then dividing by $(-7),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(y+3)^{2}+63 & =62 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2}+63-63 & =62-63 \\\\ -7(y+3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{(-1)}{(-7)} \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{(y+3)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{7}} \\\\ |y+3| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\ y+3 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\ y & =-3\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141826/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c872e855-895e-5369-8a79-cbdf21133548"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141826"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112589/selection/18782aa9bead12b63fdf0ddcc54e2f562673d49345c02e85292f010db1f3b2e4" :answer/id #uuid "830384d5-feb4-5a39-8430-8ae0528c4aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112589/selection/cf596c0dfdf10ba63029818a08c3ce4a639b2d7304a40e4b538eec61ce8c19e3" :answer/id #uuid "08e3aafb-ac51-5782-9859-1b03eca852a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112589/selection/d41c21d3f06f1be0ccf718a034d346e23fa328288ce6f02a9e57757e049fd1e7" :answer/id #uuid "24f399a0-a029-535e-83d5-fa8546550f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112589/selection/c24f4b3947f5117359a1aef8a8ce173476fae9cfb5ebaf32f90d74469dfd1b00" :answer/id #uuid "f4f9cd0a-3390-52df-bf95-5c83e0bbde87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112589/selection/75ac4cdde302156f7af2f12ad905114a12b2aab151a43ca9e3019402f12217f3" :answer/id #uuid "98c6b69f-1c00-5f85-8930-463d7fd5fc27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=\\frac{25}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112589/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5270b5b1-ad42-54b5-b62a-7647ac25035d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112589/selection/18782aa9bead12b63fdf0ddcc54e2f562673d49345c02e85292f010db1f3b2e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-112589/selection/18782aa9bead12b63fdf0ddcc54e2f562673d49345c02e85292f010db1f3b2e4" "q-112589/selection/cf596c0dfdf10ba63029818a08c3ce4a639b2d7304a40e4b538eec61ce8c19e3" "q-112589/selection/d41c21d3f06f1be0ccf718a034d346e23fa328288ce6f02a9e57757e049fd1e7" "q-112589/selection/c24f4b3947f5117359a1aef8a8ce173476fae9cfb5ebaf32f90d74469dfd1b00" "q-112589/selection/75ac4cdde302156f7af2f12ad905114a12b2aab151a43ca9e3019402f12217f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112589" :question/id #uuid "6aac66b0-f320-570c-a0da-d85c24be6410" :question/math-academy-id "q-112589" :question/problem "The equation $6{z}^{2}+10z-1=0$ can be written in the form $6(z+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{z}^{2}+10z-1 & =0 \\\\ 6{z}^{2}+10z & =1 \\\\ 6({z}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}z) & =1 \\\\ 6[{z}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}\\cdot z+{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}] & =1 \\\\ 6[{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}] & =1 \\\\ 6[{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{25}{36}] & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{25}{36} & =1 \\\\ 6{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{25}{6} & =1 \\\\ 6{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} & =\\frac{31}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{5}{6}$ and $q=\\frac{31}{6}.$ Finally,\n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{31}{6}=\\frac{36}{6}=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112589/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "257b907c-70c1-5bbd-a6d2-297d51325d1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112524/selection/18782aa9bead12b63fdf0ddcc54e2f562673d49345c02e85292f010db1f3b2e4" :answer/id #uuid "50733610-6584-5c7a-8b1e-6e5660fb9295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112524/selection/4f4c97ecc85d3676e2bca3b719629897a174632f70f43e72d499d57349e6a10b" :answer/id #uuid "fd8d7f44-707e-55f3-9c12-01966637e3e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112524/selection/5c885b0462216dbe9522312267c8911f03a34a5e17506b2be59716a9d8165bbe" :answer/id #uuid "e01afa12-4587-5034-ad2a-fef717b93d97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112524/selection/cd05a9c879fe7c7ee9b8026c9d1a4dd62cddc1b9cc1450cb8c6ed4b3570b8d46" :answer/id #uuid "136be8ce-1bc9-5ee4-a4c1-5c2c4748161f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112524/selection/9121211b46456cdf6d538c26fec8832f84e25f2ee2e024bcde14b0ebbcdb7efe" :answer/id #uuid "f2680221-28cf-541f-beef-5887d3ea2f88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112524/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8715488d-6b94-5790-b869-f7dcd004f51e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112524/selection/cd05a9c879fe7c7ee9b8026c9d1a4dd62cddc1b9cc1450cb8c6ed4b3570b8d46" :answer-field/choices ["q-112524/selection/18782aa9bead12b63fdf0ddcc54e2f562673d49345c02e85292f010db1f3b2e4" "q-112524/selection/4f4c97ecc85d3676e2bca3b719629897a174632f70f43e72d499d57349e6a10b" "q-112524/selection/5c885b0462216dbe9522312267c8911f03a34a5e17506b2be59716a9d8165bbe" "q-112524/selection/cd05a9c879fe7c7ee9b8026c9d1a4dd62cddc1b9cc1450cb8c6ed4b3570b8d46" "q-112524/selection/9121211b46456cdf6d538c26fec8832f84e25f2ee2e024bcde14b0ebbcdb7efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112524" :question/id #uuid "eaa71aa3-e92b-5db0-96a6-7043b42bf47f" :question/math-academy-id "q-112524" :question/problem "The equation $4{x}^{2}+6x-5=0$ can be written in the form $4(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+6x-5 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+6x & =5 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}x) & =5 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot x+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}] & =5 \\\\ 4[{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}] & =5 \\\\ 4[{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{16}] & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{9}{16} & =5 \\\\ 4{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4} & =5 \\\\ 4{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{29}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{3}{4}$ and $q=\\frac{29}{4}.$ Finally,\n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{29}{4}=\\frac{32}{4}=8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112524/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "257b907c-70c1-5bbd-a6d2-297d51325d1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-60352/selection/a23f1e617a086ffa629299cf71c4b51f3ea6de833bb28974dbaafa976391510e" :answer/id #uuid "6ce4de43-f249-510d-a656-c4fa87cd5633" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60352/selection/728e252d95d7ffaa9cc1add5ad1b0d468423b2d116cccaac168fb42afc10a7f5" :answer/id #uuid "d47020a1-a0fb-5f41-89b8-8d2adef7e6d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60352/selection/d02dab6b572c9be535131f83a7f96275e8e78843ee66f19d2df7bffac644b66d" :answer/id #uuid "4f1ccf6e-e73b-5e00-945f-154138118549" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60352/selection/9ea6e494145b147641880080335213ed72f164642d95e9aec985faa267dcc755" :answer/id #uuid "d8ba41fe-f143-5413-8280-d53f83092a93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60352/selection/f9fa030f6977cafc43abdbeb261c7e6d9f41518fd9f635b00400c6a88f14a54d" :answer/id #uuid "dcbce261-8163-51ae-8064-58acdc80df9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60352/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac16ef78-5772-5932-b805-b46c06811599" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-60352/selection/728e252d95d7ffaa9cc1add5ad1b0d468423b2d116cccaac168fb42afc10a7f5" :answer-field/choices ["q-60352/selection/a23f1e617a086ffa629299cf71c4b51f3ea6de833bb28974dbaafa976391510e" "q-60352/selection/728e252d95d7ffaa9cc1add5ad1b0d468423b2d116cccaac168fb42afc10a7f5" "q-60352/selection/d02dab6b572c9be535131f83a7f96275e8e78843ee66f19d2df7bffac644b66d" "q-60352/selection/9ea6e494145b147641880080335213ed72f164642d95e9aec985faa267dcc755" "q-60352/selection/f9fa030f6977cafc43abdbeb261c7e6d9f41518fd9f635b00400c6a88f14a54d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-60352" :question/id #uuid "5b84d7df-0101-52b9-a6f9-9e8e6ac2509d" :question/math-academy-id "q-60352" :question/problem "The equation $3{x}^{2}-4x+1=0$ can be written in the form $3(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-4x+1 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4x & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4x & =-1 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}x) & =-1 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}x+{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}] & =-1 \\\\ 3[{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{4}{9}] & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}-3\\cdot \\frac{4}{9} & =-1 \\\\ 3{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3} & =-1 \\\\ 3{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} & =-1+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 3{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $q=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-60352/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "257b907c-70c1-5bbd-a6d2-297d51325d1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-60352"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-60360"] :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4x-9 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-4x & =9 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-2x) & =9 \\\\ 2[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{(1)}^{2}-{(1)}^{2}] & =9 \\\\ 2[{(x-1)}^{2}-1] & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(x-1)}^{2}-2\\cdot 1 & =9 \\\\ 2{(x-1)}^{2}-2 & =9 \\\\ 2{(x-1)}^{2} & =9+2 \\\\ 2{(x-1)}^{2} & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $q=11.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(x-1)}^{2} & =11 \\\\ {(x-1)}^{2} & =\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-1)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{2}} \\\\ |x-1| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{2}} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{2}} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-60361/selection/db29474676d4ff23c441e3054cce025032905ca11c6d53f27f70dc830d004528" :answer/id #uuid "f322e9b6-a8a3-5cc2-a213-1911c5985c34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{4},\\,x=\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{21}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60361/selection/85606ba1dad330a704e70f5793b30f3bb37e967f4b55407dc2100cc8dbc88ba2" :answer/id #uuid "cb0cf68c-c133-5a7a-ba61-bf9c174a7ded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{21}{4},\\,x=\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{21}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60361/selection/8908beb2df0b2e68ddb92b5a6ea5839238a50a5198b11f0cff27495dbfe4e5cb" :answer/id #uuid "1dc6e53b-99ac-5d0d-97b0-03d08208cc10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{3}{4},\\,x=\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{21}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60361/selection/9db91d2caccd039083ffd82009a816f75523ec9e5181b87f12820c69f9506fd1" :answer/id #uuid "8252e8a8-8e94-558a-9d3b-5ad687bb1f8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=\\frac{21}{4},\\,x=\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{21}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60361/selection/5d8b49c79c3db58b7e8a97054dbbfe6c7266ecdd31aafd566af9c2448bf2b906" :answer/id #uuid "e441a9da-cd57-539e-b157-792c43f282b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{3}{4},\\,x=\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{21}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60361/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec00c36-7df0-5623-aaa6-dd0b8fb470e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-60361/selection/8908beb2df0b2e68ddb92b5a6ea5839238a50a5198b11f0cff27495dbfe4e5cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-60361/selection/db29474676d4ff23c441e3054cce025032905ca11c6d53f27f70dc830d004528" "q-60361/selection/85606ba1dad330a704e70f5793b30f3bb37e967f4b55407dc2100cc8dbc88ba2" "q-60361/selection/8908beb2df0b2e68ddb92b5a6ea5839238a50a5198b11f0cff27495dbfe4e5cb" "q-60361/selection/9db91d2caccd039083ffd82009a816f75523ec9e5181b87f12820c69f9506fd1" "q-60361/selection/5d8b49c79c3db58b7e8a97054dbbfe6c7266ecdd31aafd566af9c2448bf2b906"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-60361" :question/id #uuid "9b5fd573-7977-528c-826a-5b51ee59aaa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-60361" :question/problem "The equation $4{x}^{2}-6x-3=0$ can be written in the form $4(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-6x-3 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-6x & =3 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}x] & =3 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}x+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}] & =3 \\\\ 4[{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{16}] & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{9}{16} & =3 \\\\ 4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4} & =3 \\\\ 4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =3+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{21}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-\\frac{3}{4}.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{21}{4} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{21}{16} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{16}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{3}{4}| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{16}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{4} & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{21}{16}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{4} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{4}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{21}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-60361/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "257b907c-70c1-5bbd-a6d2-297d51325d1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-60361"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-60356/selection/c20a65bce07cef48f81ab72b9e1ade1a044a10b95f5e8446eadf52a8ae56da38" :answer/id #uuid "e1770bdf-8d9f-571b-ae40-d4f91c8d8388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q-p=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60356/selection/425322f40303d82ceaeed67bba89c1b251b1f36a788e5865555f5683c92ef142" :answer/id #uuid "00f13bc1-ef94-5fd7-ab6b-765c5a7be483" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q-p=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60356/selection/6a6d3502e6a65d36f6f546cfa067146bfb5fc56cf79cf05b2ea13599275ed302" :answer/id #uuid "b972c7fa-8a32-58b2-8501-8f2c0b540d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q-p=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60356/selection/7b643c4f043753f01c4e407bc81ba45445b040b5bf3b7e91766cbe3e4559feb4" :answer/id #uuid "61f8af42-ceca-58dd-84be-cdf0b71cb880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q-p=\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60356/selection/97d0ef1f9d7a48949fc6b48a4f6235b3eb267c70e36d89f9145b2c7e269bd726" :answer/id #uuid "eb726894-2bf1-569b-b85f-83bd3bccfe74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q-p=\\frac{17}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-60356/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "82e2dbc8-909e-53b1-8aa0-9b05150128a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-60356/selection/c20a65bce07cef48f81ab72b9e1ade1a044a10b95f5e8446eadf52a8ae56da38" :answer-field/choices ["q-60356/selection/c20a65bce07cef48f81ab72b9e1ade1a044a10b95f5e8446eadf52a8ae56da38" "q-60356/selection/425322f40303d82ceaeed67bba89c1b251b1f36a788e5865555f5683c92ef142" "q-60356/selection/6a6d3502e6a65d36f6f546cfa067146bfb5fc56cf79cf05b2ea13599275ed302" "q-60356/selection/7b643c4f043753f01c4e407bc81ba45445b040b5bf3b7e91766cbe3e4559feb4" "q-60356/selection/97d0ef1f9d7a48949fc6b48a4f6235b3eb267c70e36d89f9145b2c7e269bd726"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-60356" :question/id #uuid "a7884f70-6bc5-5884-9b9e-474178b4363b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60356" :question/problem "The equation $-3{x}^{2}-2x+6=0$ can be written in the form $3(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q-p.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}-2x+6) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x-6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+2x-6 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x & =6 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}x] & =6 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}x+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}] & =6 \\\\ 3[{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{9}] & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{9} & =6 \\\\ 3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3} & =6 \\\\ 3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & =6+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & =\\frac{19}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{1}{3}$, $q=\\frac{19}{3}.$ Finally,\n\n$$\nq-p=\\frac{19}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{18}{3}=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-60356/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-60356"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "eaee1ee0-16b6-5ac8-9684-ccafb3514b10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f3f601a-a2ed-5971-a838-18aac0264706" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218774/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-218774/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "af5c0f70-2948-511c-a755-1c2452c06a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e347caf-2f67-5f8d-bc13-f8ad3a4df261" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218774/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-218774/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4b991bb5-f47f-5d38-8b61-f286a0dc0a20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea5250e-320f-58f1-8227-d9762f35a7ae" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218774/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-218774/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-4/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a" :answer/id #uuid "656063bd-cb30-59e7-816b-19d5e5b298ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "05ce2aef-e5cd-5238-a3a2-60f589d93192" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-218774/field-4/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a" :answer-field/choices ["q-218774/field-4/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-218774" :question/id #uuid "5e7106f2-d83d-5e6e-ab69-f66cab3f2fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-218774" :question/problem "$$\n-4{x}^{2}+16x-11=0\n$$\n\nBy completing the square, the above equation is equivalent to$\\,\\,4(x\\,\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}, and the solutions are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-3}}\n$\\pm $\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{x}^{2}+16x-11) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-16x+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-16x+11 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-16x & =-11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-4x) & =-11 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{(2)}^{2}-{(2)}^{2}] & =-11 \\\\ 4[{(x-2)}^{2}-4] & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-2)}^{2}-4\\cdot 4 & =-11 \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2}-16 & =-11 \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2} & =16-11 \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-2)}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {(x-2)}^{2} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-2)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{4}} \\\\ |x-2| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\ |x-2| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\\\ x & =2\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-218774/field-1" "q-218774/field-2" "q-218774/field-3" "q-218774/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-218774"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86413/selection/ea4cdcb83fbda2b652d13fb3cc3ae34edb26862265d08af6d9c3804e0dc34513" :answer/id #uuid "a0725f26-a759-5a49-abb2-057d9c90d3d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=12,\\,w=-2\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86413/selection/0f81fe3dd860c8152cc5c69aa8d303e4eeca57332181a767704a627ae8622e62" :answer/id #uuid "faeb6088-4e17-5f4c-ad2b-39eefaee2523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=12,\\,w=\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86413/selection/73be9161b37fd0d93455b7e616e958eb44aa78b0d68e0a6a234ec105448f0661" :answer/id #uuid "777afa51-6d00-5595-9dcb-91e413702e61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=2,\\,w=\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86413/selection/ec72fdf6bc8070ee5e06e807b0dda6659ff7bd51da13e31d91e2e95fed1f6473" :answer/id #uuid "0aeaa9e5-509a-50dc-8baf-a50a1a248749" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=12,\\,w=-\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86413/selection/7a8ebb2aa6b2c84cc497d2c3c949c21c526a4469a94656e5ad7f3815482849d7" :answer/id #uuid "0238612d-81df-54c7-b32a-2859875c2ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=2,\\,w=-\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86413/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb4db1c-26d6-50fa-8abd-decddeb3a678" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86413/selection/ec72fdf6bc8070ee5e06e807b0dda6659ff7bd51da13e31d91e2e95fed1f6473" :answer-field/choices ["q-86413/selection/ea4cdcb83fbda2b652d13fb3cc3ae34edb26862265d08af6d9c3804e0dc34513" "q-86413/selection/0f81fe3dd860c8152cc5c69aa8d303e4eeca57332181a767704a627ae8622e62" "q-86413/selection/73be9161b37fd0d93455b7e616e958eb44aa78b0d68e0a6a234ec105448f0661" "q-86413/selection/ec72fdf6bc8070ee5e06e807b0dda6659ff7bd51da13e31d91e2e95fed1f6473" "q-86413/selection/7a8ebb2aa6b2c84cc497d2c3c949c21c526a4469a94656e5ad7f3815482849d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86413" :question/id #uuid "7895edb1-f2c2-5302-ad9e-dc0b6ea9c033" :question/math-academy-id "q-86413" :question/problem "The equation $-4{w}^{2}-4w+11=0$ can be written in the form $4(w+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{w}^{2}-4w+11) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}+4w-11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{w}^{2}+4w-11 & =0 \\\\ 4({w}^{2}+w) & =11 \\\\ 4[{w}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}w+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}] & =11 \\\\ 4[{(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}] & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} & =11 \\\\ 4{(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-1 & =11 \\\\ 4{(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =11+1 \\\\ 4{(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q=12.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{12}{4} \\\\ {(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{{(w+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |w+\\frac{1}{2}| & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ w+\\frac{1}{2} & =\\pm \\sqrt{3} \\\\ w & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86413/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86413"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86412/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "e2b426b7-8c01-5060-bc7d-7f8e33e09ec3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86412/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "e5b653f4-3eb2-5f2f-8d08-28c70a39ed73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86412/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "98e69c8c-2c87-5e41-a994-06b8f335cd45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86412/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "418db140-8c84-53a5-be6c-55ecf437ef76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86412/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "e3fcce2a-acce-542b-9c9a-2e874a0f56aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86412/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bb2a0dd-95d7-58f8-a9c0-2a2fd34ad13a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86412/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-86412/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-86412/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-86412/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-86412/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-86412/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86412" :question/id #uuid "a4e2f4d5-6f49-50f5-b088-915973bd5e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-86412" :question/problem "The equation $-2{x}^{2}+12x-9=0$ can be written in the form $2(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-2{x}^{2}+12x-9) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-12x+9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-12x+9 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-12x & =-9 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-6x) & =-9 \\\\ 2[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =-9 \\\\ 2[{(x-3)}^{2}-9] & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(x-3)}^{2}-2\\cdot 9 & =-9 \\\\ 2{(x-3)}^{2}-18 & =-9 \\\\ 2{(x-3)}^{2} & =-9+18 \\\\ 2{(x-3)}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3$ and $q=9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86412/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112607/selection/da6302beca8341ba8539eab3041b697899aa66466d582876ac3be7f70211f896" :answer/id #uuid "a1c50d6e-d908-53c5-9e0c-2e5d6517bc8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=3,\\,x=-4\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112607/selection/6440463c0e9dc8d50b3991c205e3c0c3e6db0bb022418f11a447aa49f287f33b" :answer/id #uuid "e25b65f3-dbce-5182-aca5-264108bbcc8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-4,\\,x=-4\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112607/selection/ba82d36addcdfc840e593b8774aaa58b6da080418db2337bafa9e61c764d26e4" :answer/id #uuid "10b99919-c2b2-54ca-89a9-16dad9d82ef7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=3,\\,x=-1\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112607/selection/0da83caa2cfc3b89322438b9971a07dc4b63ab24d4f340c65d542f5d19ceb35a" :answer/id #uuid "16870299-2ab5-5fbc-a81d-251c616efc8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=3,\\,x=-6\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112607/selection/8c0c618b9c456056679aa36de5626bcc05d3a043e72b841d9c031f4c9b39b774" :answer/id #uuid "270f4210-6715-5e8a-93e8-9fd28c4601b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q=-4,\\,x=-3\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae379b48-545b-5df5-8beb-dcf5df2a8c84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112607/selection/da6302beca8341ba8539eab3041b697899aa66466d582876ac3be7f70211f896" :answer-field/choices ["q-112607/selection/da6302beca8341ba8539eab3041b697899aa66466d582876ac3be7f70211f896" "q-112607/selection/6440463c0e9dc8d50b3991c205e3c0c3e6db0bb022418f11a447aa49f287f33b" "q-112607/selection/ba82d36addcdfc840e593b8774aaa58b6da080418db2337bafa9e61c764d26e4" "q-112607/selection/0da83caa2cfc3b89322438b9971a07dc4b63ab24d4f340c65d542f5d19ceb35a" "q-112607/selection/8c0c618b9c456056679aa36de5626bcc05d3a043e72b841d9c031f4c9b39b774"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112607" :question/id #uuid "f0fbec27-7172-503f-a463-3fab8b8173d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-112607" :question/problem "The equation $-4{x}^{2}-32x-61=0$ can be written in the form $4(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{x}^{2}-32x-61) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+32x+61 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+32x+61 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+32x & =-61 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+8x) & =-61 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2}] & =-61 \\\\ 4[{(x+4)}^{2}-16] & =-61\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x+4)}^{2}-4\\cdot 16 & =-61 \\\\ 4{(x+4)}^{2}-64 & =-61 \\\\ 4{(x+4)}^{2} & =-61+64 \\\\ 4{(x+4)}^{2} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q=3.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x+4)}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {(x+4)}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x+4)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ |x+4| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ x & =-4\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3996c79f-9281-5b9d-9b33-8863f10adc33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
